\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Sector selection and compatibility}
\date{2026-11-08}

\p{The binary tetrahedral datum of \ref{fdip-00A1} has real
coefficient field and fiber
##{F=(\mathbb C^2)_{\mathbb R}\oplus\mathbb R^3,\qquad
T(g)=\rho_s^{\mathbb R}(g)\oplus\tau(g).}
Its invariant real inner product is the direct sum of the real
part of the spinor's standard Hermitian metric and the rotation
fiber's Euclidean metric, the two metrics specified in \ref{fdip-007K}.
The group, representation and trivial action on the finite graph are supplied.}

\p{The real group algebra #{\mathbb R[2T]} and
#{\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb R}(F)} are associative unital
[real algebras](ca-0016), with no commutativity assumption on their
multiplication. The central idempotent #{e_-=(1-[z])/2} of
\ref{fgap-0015} selects a sector through this supplied representation;
the distinguished central involution #{z} corresponds to the
quaternion #{-1} under the comparison in \ref{fdip-00A0}.
Its image #{P} retains the real spinor summand. The effect on the
named operator #{T(g)}, namely that #{PT(g)P} keeps its spinor
block and removes its rotation block, is proved in \ref{fdip-00A1}.}

\p{The constructed comparisons are
#{\pi:SU(2)\to SO(3)} and the induced map #{2T\to A_4}, with
kernel #{\{1,-1\}}, as proved in \ref{fdip-00A0}.
They recover the tetrahedral rotation representation. The
covariant Dirac construction in \ref{fdip-009N} still requires a Clifford
module and its compatibility with any spin-frame action, separately
from an internal action or an action on the graph. The quaternion
identities alone supply no such intertwiner; the
larger correspondences in \ref{fdip-00A2} remain open.}

\p{The [sufficient Gaussian data map](fdip-005E) retains a positive
precision and a declared Euclidean metric as well as the projector;
together these determine the retained law. The representation and sector
above supply no such precision. Supplied, selected and derived
are mathematical roles, independent of the symmetry, bubble
initial-conditions and local-environment questions in the
[motivation](fdip-00AU). Sector projection supplies no dynamical
symmetry-breaking or vacuum-selection law.}
